<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masindi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masindi is a town in western Uganda, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-albert">Lake Albert</a>. In the nineteenth century it was a royal centre of Omukama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a> of Bunyoro. In 1872 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-baker">Samuel Baker</a>, acting for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khedive-of-egypt">Khedive of Egypt</a>, proclaimed the annexation of Bunyoro there, but Kabalega's forces attacked and drove him out. It is now the centre of a district of the same name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masindi.jpg" alt="Masindi" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JabbarYunus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masindi,_Uganda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
